Make the following edits to `/tmp/sv-12c61294e69844bcb0325acec755c8a4/before/Common/Custom/Models/ManagedServiceIdentity.Serialization.cs` to fix AOT warnings.

### Fix 1: Line 31 - Replace `JsonSerializer.Serialize(writer, ManagedServiceIdentityType, jOptions)`

This line uses JsonSerializer to serialize ManagedServiceIdentityType which has a custom JsonConverter. The converter just writes `"type"` property name and the string value. For V3 converter, "SystemAssigned, UserAssigned" becomes "SystemAssigned,UserAssigned" (no space).

Replace:
```csharp
            JsonSerializer.Serialize(writer, ManagedServiceIdentityType, jOptions);
```
with:
```csharp
            writer.WritePropertyName("type"u8);
            bool useV3Value = false;
            if (jOptions != null && ManagedServiceIdentityType == ManagedServiceIdentityType.SystemAssignedUserAssigned)
            {
                foreach (var converter in jOptions.Converters)
                {
                    if (converter is ManagedServiceIdentityTypeV3Converter)
                    {
                        useV3Value = true;
                        break;
                    }
                }
            }
            writer.WriteStringValue(useV3Value ? ManagedServiceIdentityTypeV3Converter.SystemAssignedUserAssignedV3Value : ManagedServiceIdentityType.ToString());
```

### Fix 2: Line 49 - Replace `JsonSerializer.Serialize(writer, item.Value, jOptions)`

UserAssignedIdentity implements IJsonModel<UserAssignedIdentity>, so use WriteObjectValue instead.

Replace:
```csharp
                    JsonSerializer.Serialize(writer, item.Value, jOptions);
```
with:
```csharp
                    writer.WriteObjectValue(item.Value, ModelSerializationExtensions.WireOptions);
```

### Fix 3: Line 206 - Replace `JsonSerializer.Deserialize<ManagedServiceIdentityType>($"{{{property}}}")`

This creates a JSON string like `{"type":"SystemAssigned"}` and deserializes it. The converter reads the "type" property value. Since we're already in the handler for the "type" property, the value is in `property.Value`.

Replace:
```csharp
                    type = JsonSerializer.Deserialize<ManagedServiceIdentityType>($"{{{property}}}");
